This project is an independent, unofficial reimplementation. It is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Mark of the Unicorn, Inc.

"MOTU", "CueMix", "PCIe-424", "HD192", "2408mk3" and "24I/O" are trademarks of
Mark of the Unicorn, Inc., used here only to identify the hardware and software
this project interoperates with.

The MIT licence above covers this project's own source code. It does not, and
cannot, cover MOTU's material:

  - MOTU's audio driver (MOTUPCIAudio.kext, including the HALPlugin it
    contains) is NOT distributed here. It must be obtained from MOTU and
    installed separately. This project calls into it; it neither includes nor
    modifies it.

  - assets/classic contains sprites from MOTU's CueMix FX, and docs/reference
    contains screenshots of MOTU's applications. These remain MOTU's copyright,
    are included only so this project can present the interface those users
    already know, and are NOT licensed under the MIT terms above.

    The Classic skin does not depend on them being here: the app reads the same
    artwork at runtime from a copy of CueMix FX the user has installed, and
    falls back to the Modern skin, which is this project's own work, if none is
    found. See assets/classic/README.md.

  - The application icons in assets/icons are original work, generated by
    tools/mkicon.m.

If Mark of the Unicorn, Inc. would prefer their material not be redistributed
here, contact the author and it will be removed; the runtime path above means
nothing is lost by doing so.

Interface descriptions in docs/ were produced by examining publicly shipped
binaries in order to interoperate with hardware the author owns.

JUCE, included as a submodule under third_party/, is licensed separately by
Raw Material Software Limited under its own terms.
